# Copy this file to .secrets (repo root, gitignored) and fill in your values.
# act reads this file automatically when running from the repo root.
#
# ── Minimum required ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# GITHUB_TOKEN is all you need for LLM to work in act tests.
# The fallback chain in scraut.yml uses GitHub Models (gpt-4o-mini) automatically
# when the primary provider has no key — so LLM calls return real output, not "".
#
#   Get it with:   gh auth token
#   Or create one: https://github.com/settings/tokens  (no scopes needed for Models)
#
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ── Optional: primary provider keys ─────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Set one of these to test with your preferred LLM provider instead of the
# github fallback. If set, the primary provider is used; fallback is skipped.
#
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# ── Optional: Slack notification steps ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# Only needed if you want to test Slack posting. dry_run=true skips posts anyway.
#
SLACK_WEBHOOK=
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=

# ── Using Ollama (fully offline, no API key needed) ──────────────────────────
#
# To use Ollama as the LLM in act tests instead of GitHub Models:
#
#   1. Install and start Ollama on your Mac:
#        brew install ollama
#        ollama serve          (keep running in background)
#        ollama pull qwen2.5:0.5b   (394 MB, only once)
#
#   2. Edit workspace/scraut.yml to point at the Docker-visible host address:
#        llm:
#          provider: ollama
#          model: qwen2.5:0.5b
#          base_url: http://host.docker.internal:11434
#
#   No secret key needed — Ollama has no auth.
